! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: some trainers lack collaborators and carry training delivery alone.

  + context: Minted by library-loop problem-authoring batch A5 from the committed UKRN training manuscript.
  + IF:
    Sustained training delivery depends on collaboration with relevant peers.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the independent committed source: “However, not all participants felt they had the same opportunities for collaboration. Some participants described limited access to relevant peers, and being seen as the only person responsible for training delivery.” (source: futon5a essays/ukrn-open-research-training-plos-one/ukrn-open-research-training-plos-one-v2.5-submission.md:183)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer the missing-contribution-access problem.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source states the collaboration and single-person-responsibility failure before the library patterns propose contribution pathways.
